'''Ka'aÿra''' (from {{Langx|tpn|ka'a-y-ra}}; {{Literal translation|where the forest and water meet|forest-water place}}) is a [[Cantons of Balisca|canton]]-city that serves as the [[Cites in Balisca|administrative and cultural center]] of the indigenous [[Pindorama]] [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|nation]], the northernmost [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Balisca]]. Per the [[2025 Baliscan census]], the city had a [[W:Population|population]] of 1,003,216. 

Ka'aÿra is located on the [[Altiplano (Pindorama)|''Altiplano'']] of Pindorama, the largest highland plain within Balisca. The modern city was officially founded on 6 November 1811. Before that, Ka'aÿra had been for centuries one of the most important and populous sites in Pindorama. 

